***

▢ Enhance the selection experience for animated element. 

** Problem: 
Currently, when we select an animated item, the selection box is drawn but the element keep moving, which create a weird UX experience when trying to move, resize it. The selection box is drawn over a region that seems empty.

** Idea and solution:
• Detect if the element have some animation attached to it.
• If no, proceed to the current usual behavior for the selection.
• If yes, create a semi transparent overlay that cover everything on the svg, with a small button "quit" at the bottom left corner. And on top of this overlay, create a static (not animated) duplicate of the targeted shape at its original position (without the attached animation). We would need logic to strip the element from the outter anim-wrapper and duplicate only the element.
• The static duplicate shape should contain a reference to the original animated shape, and to it's outter wrapping-group <g>, which contains the matrix transformations.
• We would still see the animated original under the overlay, and the overlay would act as a click blocker to facilitate the shape resizing and translating by the user.


